Z||000000||moonie||02-25-2001||05:39 PM||||85 se 2.5l 4 cyl iron duke<P>i finally put a head on that i got from a local junkyard. everything went pretty smooth except for a m9inor things.<P>when i tried to start it ,the fuel pump didn't click on. it turned over OK soi shot it with a little ether. fired right up. i kept it running with ether for about 90 seconds. i missed a shot & motor died.<BR>so...i shot it with ether & ran around to turn the key & the motor will not turn over. when the starter hits....it makes a LOUD clunking noise & i can hear a slight whining noise. the lights & windshield wipers work <BR>( was thinking about little ire on starter )<BR>but the engine will not turn over. the clunking noise sounds like its coming from inside the intake manifold , but i'mnot real sure <P>any thoughts on what todo next ??????<BR>thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-25-2001||07:31 PM||||Check your battery connections and make sure that they're good. Another possibility is that the starter locked up on you. If you feel that the engine may have locked up on you, try turning it by hand-key OFF!||||reg||1
